{"name":"Golden Moray Eel","hex":"#ffcf60","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"moray","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the large cosmopolitan carnivorous eels of the family Muraenidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moray"},{"term":"eel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any freshwater fish of the order Anguilliformes, which are elongated and resemble snakes.","A European eel (Anguilla anguilla)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for eels.","To move with a sinuous motion like that of an eel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gymnothorax miliaris","blocks":[{"text":"Gymnothorax miliaris, the goldentail moray, bastard eel, or conger moray, is a species of marine fish in the family Muraenidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Gymnothorax_miliaris_%28goldentail_moray_eel%29_%28San_Salvador_Island%2C_Bahamas%29_3_%2816171148365%29.jpg/330px-Gymnothorax_miliaris_%28goldentail_moray_eel%29_%28San_Salvador_Island%2C_Bahamas%29_3_%2816171148365%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gymnothorax_miliaris","wikidata":"Q2971678"},{"title":"Moray eel","blocks":[{"text":"Moray eels, or Muraenidae, are a family of eels whose members are found worldwide. There are approximately 200 species in 16 genera which are almost exclusively marine, but several species are regularly seen in brackish water, and a few are found in fresh water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Moray_eel.jpg/330px-Moray_eel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moray_eel","wikidata":"Q35076"},{"title":"Moray","blocks":[{"text":"Moray is one of the 32 council areas of Scotland. It lies in the north-east of the country, with a coastline on the Moray Firth, and borders the council areas of Aberdeenshire and Highland. Its council is based in Elgin, the area's largest town. The main towns are generally in the north of the area on the coastal plain. The south of the area is more sparsely populated and mountainous, including part of the Cairngorms National Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Moray_UK_location_map.svg/330px-Moray_UK_location_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moray","wikidata":"Q211106"},{"title":"Eel","blocks":[{"text":"Eels are ray-finned fish belonging to the order Anguilliformes, which consists of eight suborders, 20 families, 164 genera, and about 1000 species. Eels undergo considerable development from the early larval stage to the eventual adult stage and are usually predators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/New_Zealand_longfin_eel_%28Anguilla_dieffenbachii%29_Piha.jpg/330px-New_Zealand_longfin_eel_%28Anguilla_dieffenbachii%29_Piha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eel","wikidata":"Q128685"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Gymnothorax_miliaris_%28goldentail_moray_eel%29_%28San_Salvador_Island%2C_Bahamas%29_3_%2816171148365%29.jpg/500px-Gymnothorax_miliaris_%28goldentail_moray_eel%29_%28San_Salvador_Island%2C_Bahamas%29_3_%2816171148365%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c